From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: report the TP port on the copper 10G PHYs

The C45 ability reader genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities() fills the supported
link-mode mask with Autoneg and the speeds but leaves the TP/MII port bits
alone; only the C22 genphy_read_abilities() sets them.  ethtool derives
"Supported ports" from those bits, not from phydev->port, so a C45-only PHY
that never adds them reports an empty list while "Port: Twisted Pair" is
correct - the port type comes from the phy core's medium - and the two
lines contradict each other.

On the XR1710G both 10G ports are RTL8261BE (mdio 08 and 05, both driven by
rtl826x_get_features()) and both report

    Supported ports: [ ]

next to a full 100M/1G/2.5G/5G/10G speed list.  rtl822x_c45_get_features()
already sets the TP bit after the same C45 read; the RTL8261 helpers never
did.

Every part on rtl826x_get_features() (RTL8261BE, RTL8261N, RTL8264,
RTL8264B) and on rtl8261x_get_features() (RTL8261C/D/CE) is copper, so set
ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT once the abilities are known.  The supported speed
mask, the advertisement, MDI/X and the data path are untouched.

Check after flashing: ethtool wan | grep 'Supported ports' -> [ TP ], and
the "Supported link modes" list is the same as before.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -520,16 +520,22 @@
 
 static int rtl8261x_get_features(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/* RTL8261C/D/CE are copper as well; the C45 abilities carry no port
+	 * type and the common helper does not add one.
+	 */
+	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	/*
 	 * Supplement Multi-Gig speeds that may not be automatically detected
 	 * RTL8261X supports 2.5G/5G in addition to standard 10G
 	 */
 	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_2500baseT_Full_BIT,
 			 phydev->supported);
 	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_5000baseT_Full_BIT,
 			 phydev->supported);
@@ -3997,16 +4003,23 @@
 static int rtl826x_get_features(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities() reports no port type: the C45
+	 * helper sets Autoneg and the speeds only, unlike the C22
+	 * genphy_read_abilities(). Every part driven by this helper is
+	 * copper, so say so and let ethtool print "Supported ports: [ TP ]".
+	 */
+	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	/* not support 10M modes */
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Half_BIT,
 			   phydev->supported);
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Full_BIT,
 			   phydev->supported);
 
 	return 0;
 }
